ap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-05T00:00:00+00:00"},{"id":51173,"front":"<p>She ________ed tomatoes and herbs in the garden every spring. (\u00fcltet \/ el\u00fcltet)<\/p><p>The factory ________ was shut down due to safety violations. (\u00fczem \/ gy\u00e1r)<\/p><p>Someone had ________ed a listening device in the office. (elhelyez \/ elrejt)<\/p><p>He ________ed a kiss on her cheek and said goodbye. (nyom \/ elhelyez)<\/p><p>\u00fcltet \/ \u00fczem \/ gy\u00e1r \/ elhelyez \/ elrejt<\/p><p>Negative meaning (HU): kiszed \/ kiv\u00e1g \/ bez\u00e1r (gy\u00e1rat)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ (noun) = n\u00f6v\u00e9ny \/ gy\u00e1r, \u00fczem<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ (verb) = el\u00fcltet \/ elhelyez \/ elrejt (titkosan)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ an idea = gondolatot \u00fcltet valakibe<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ evidence = bizony\u00edt\u00e9kot hamis\u00edt \/ elhelyez<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 power ________ = er\u0151m\u0171<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p>noun: plant<\/p><p>verb: plant<\/p><p>past tense \/ -ing form: planted \/ planting<\/p><p>common pair: plant a tree \/ power plant \/ plant evidence \/ plant an idea \/ factory plant<\/p><p>similar: shrub \/ factory \/ place \/ embed \/ sow<\/p><p>negative: uproot \/ demolish \/ close down \/ remove<\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":null,"review":{"state":"review","interval":4,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"5 nap","good":"10 nap","easy":"13 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-05T00:00:00+00:00"},{"id":51212,"front":"<p>They finally reached the ________ of the hill after two hours of climbing. (cs\u00facs \/ gerinc)<\/p><p>The wave was at its ________ just before it crashed onto the shore. (cs\u00facspont \/ tet\u0151fok)<\/p><p>The school&#039;s ________ features a golden eagle on a blue background. (c\u00edmer \/ jelk\u00e9p)<\/p><p>The bird had a bright orange ________ on top of its head. (taraj \/ tollb\u00f3bita)<\/p><p>cs\u00facs \/ gerinc \/ cs\u00facspont \/ c\u00edmer \/ taraj<\/p><p>Negative meaning (HU): v\u00f6lgy \/ m\u00e9lypont \/ alap \/ talpont<\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ of a hill \/ wave = hegy cs\u00facsa \/ hull\u00e1m teteje<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ (noun) = c\u00edmer (iskol\u00e1\u00e9, csapat\u00e9, csal\u00e1d\u00e9)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ (noun) = taraj (mad\u00e1r\u00e9) \/ tollb\u00f3bita<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 on the ________ of a wave = sikere cs\u00facs\u00e1n \/ felfut\u00f3ban<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________fallen = levert \/ cs\u00fcggedt \/ szomor\u00fa (idioma)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p>noun: crest<\/p><p>adjective: crestfallen<\/p><p>common pair: crest of a hill \/ crest of a wave \/ family crest \/ school crest \/ on the crest of<\/p><p>similar: peak \/ summit \/ top \/ emblem \/ plume<\/p><p>negative: trough \/ valley \/ bottom \/ low point<\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":null,"review":{"state":"review","interval":2,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"3 nap","good":"5 nap","easy":"7 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-13T20:54:35+00:00"},{"id":49598,"front":"<p>After standing up too quickly, I felt a bit _______ and had to sit back down. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl \/ megingott)<\/em><\/p><p>The patient reported experiencing episodes of _______, particularly when changing positions. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s \/ egyens\u00falyveszt\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>The rapid ascent in the hot air balloon induced a sense of _______ in some passengers. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s \/ lebeg\u00e9s \u00e9rz\u00e9se)<\/em><\/p><p>The swirling patterns on the canvas created a _______ effect, making it hard to focus. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00edt\u0151 \/ megd\u00f6bbent\u0151)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u0151 \/ sz\u00e9d\u00fclt \/ b\u00f3dult \/ lebeg\u0151 \/ megingott<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): stabil \/ kiegyens\u00falyozott \/ biztos<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 feeling _______ = sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u0151nek \u00e9rzi mag\u00e1t (pl. I&#039;m feeling a bit _______ today.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ in the head = fejben sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. He complained of _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ from heights = magass\u00e1gt\u00f3l val\u00f3 sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. She suffers from _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ sensation = sz\u00e9d\u00edt\u0151 \u00e9rz\u00e9s (pl. The roller coaster ride gave me a _______.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>dizzy<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>dizzy<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>dizziness<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: feeling dizzy \/ dizzy spells \/ dizzy from heights \/ dizzy head<\/span><\/p><p>similar: light-headed \/ vertiginous \/ woozy \/ giddy<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: steady \/ balanced \/ firm<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":4,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"5 nap","good":"9 nap","easy":"12 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-05T21:16:31+00:00"},{"id":51226,"front":"<p>I think I _______ my ankle playing soccer yesterday. <em>(megr\u00e1ndul \/ kibicsakl\u00f3dik)<\/em><\/p><p>The doctor advised him to rest and avoid putting weight on the _______ joint. <em>(megs\u00e9r\u00fclt \/ kificamodott)<\/em><\/p><p>Ligamentous _______ is a common sports injury, often resulting from sudden twisting or inversion of the foot. <em>(r\u00e1ndul\u00e1s \/ ficam)<\/em><\/p><p>She winced as she tried to stand, the sharp pain a clear indication that she had _______ her wrist. <em>(megr\u00e1nd\u00edtott \/ kificam\u00edtott)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">megr\u00e1ndul \/ kificamodik \/ ficamosodik \/ elcsavarodik<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): meggy\u00f3gyul \/ meger\u0151s\u00f6dik \/ felfriss\u00fcl<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ your ankle = megr\u00e1nd\u00edtani a bok\u00e1t (pl. He _______ his ankle badly.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ your wrist = megr\u00e1nd\u00edtani a csukl\u00f3t (pl. She fell and _______ her wrist.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ligament _______ = \u00edz\u00fcleti szalag s\u00e9r\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. The most common type of _______ is a ligament _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ injury = r\u00e1ndul\u00e1sos s\u00e9r\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. He has a mild _______ injury.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>sprain<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>sprain<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>sprain<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: sprained ankle \/ sprained wrist \/ sprained ligament \/ sprain injury<\/span><\/p><p>similar: twist \/ wrench \/ strain \/ dislocate<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: heal \/ recover \/ strengthen<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":1,"lapses":1,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"4 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-06T21:01:30+00:00"},{"id":51242,"front":"<p>After years of hard work, she finally achieved her _______ and opened her own bakery. <em>(gy\u0151zelem \/ siker)<\/em><\/p><p>The ancient Romans celebrated military _______ with grand parades and elaborate ceremonies. <em>(diadal \/ gy\u0151zelmi \u00fcnnep)<\/em><\/p><p>The scientific community hailed the discovery as a major _______ in the fight against the disease. <em>(\u00e1tt\u00f6r\u00e9s \/ eredm\u00e9ny)<\/em><\/p><p>The novel&#039;s climax depicts the hero&#039;s ultimate _______ over his inner demons. <em>(gy\u0151zelem \/ diadal)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">gy\u0151zelem \/ siker \/ diadal \/ eredm\u00e9ny \/ \u00e1tt\u00f6r\u00e9s<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): veres\u00e9g \/ kudarc \/ buk\u00e1s<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ of = valaminek a gy\u0151zelme\/diadala (pl. a triumph of the human spirit)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ victory = diadalmas gy\u0151zelem (pl. a hard-won triumph victory)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ over = gy\u0151zelem valami felett (pl. their triumph over adversity)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ in = siker valamiben (pl. a triumph in science)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>triumph<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>triumphant<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>triumphantly<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>triumph<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>triumph<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: hard-won triumph \/ sweet triumph \/ moral triumph \/ personal triumph<\/span><\/p><p>similar: victory \/ success \/ achievement \/ win<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: defeat \/ failure \/ loss<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"triumphant\ntriumphantly\ntriumph\ntriumph","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":2,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"3 nap","good":"5 nap","easy":"6 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-09T17:32:45+00:00"},{"id":51253,"front":"<p>The children were playing with _______ toys made of wood. <em>(egyszer\u0171 \/ alapvet\u0151)<\/em><\/p><p>The company&#039;s initial business plan was quite _______, 